{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/queues/api.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:03:57.029234Z","id":"2ca4a4849ef05fee2c87c696e63d9c3c27ea07cc8e176fa5da9c011bb97acf8e","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-27-report-queues-m1.md 'Shared shapes' lists PUT/DELETE for members and POST/DELETE for service grants but no GET for either. listMembers expects {members: [{public_id, display_name?, role}]} and listGrants {grants: [{id, name, created_at}]} (never the token or key). Until the daemon answers them, web/shell/src/queues/QueueAdmin.svelte shows 'Could not load the members' / 'service grants' and still adds, removes, creates and revokes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":40},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"367a63192b3555e28255e2100ce269688894b8be2e2b0a8bd7105a3982ea5a19"},"suggested_fix":"Add both GET routes to the shared shapes and the admin routes (crates/clax-server), with these bodies, or change these two calls to what the routes answer.","summary":"The Queues page lists members and service grants from GET /api/queues/{qid}/members and GET /api/queues/{qid}/service-grants, which the plan's shared route table does not name","tags":["queues","ui","interface","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/queues/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:03:57.029306Z","id":"db30d86895b2b63a4d809ed949c848bcc33633557ac7cb45b3f324e5e1bdd165","body":{"detail":"No route answers a queue's counts: Queue in the plan's shared shapes has none. web/shell/src/queues/Queues.svelte:37 runs countReports per queue on every load, fetching every report's comments to count them; past 20 pages the counts show with a '+'. A queue with many reports costs that many requests per visit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":33},"end":{"line":45},"content_hash":"d4f0a3c5eb89649876cc8b2a83a191157cdd3646599b469e514a17c517aeee14"},"suggested_fix":"Have GET /api/queues answer counts {open, claimed, resolved} per queue (one GROUP BY in the store) and show those.","summary":"Each queue's open/claimed/resolved counts are made by paging GET /api/queues/{qid}/reports in the browser, up to 20 pages per queue","tags":["queues","perf","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/queues/api.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:06:12.186798Z","id":"a1d3be399c87ade1dadab43db4e9f5c937fe43ad0f1036ce301d2b617a3118c9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:13d7bfb0e","summary":"Both list routes are in the plan's admin row (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-27-report-queues-m1.md, Shared shapes) for Task 2 to implement, with these shapes","supersedes":"2ca4a4849ef05fee2c87c696e63d9c3c27ea07cc8e176fa5da9c011bb97acf8e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/queues/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T07:01:58.583353Z","id":"d4c62208b1db1435a628bd9f93926d49fa466fd1fc4408d0ba3e742d49376267","body":{"detail":"ReportState (web/sdk/src/types.ts) now has fix_proposed and verified. countReports (web/shell/src/queues/model.ts:34) counts them, so the Queues page's line '3 open · 1 claimed · 9 resolved' leaves out reports waiting on a verdict and reports the reporter verified.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":47},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"fa9fcd3f82888056427c44220aacba37fc86ed2bd02a5443adad49e26feec952"},"suggested_fix":"Add 'N fix proposed' and 'N verified' to countsText, or count verified with resolved, and update model.test.ts.","summary":"countsText names open, claimed and resolved only; fix_proposed and verified reports are counted but never shown","tags":["queues","shell","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/queues/ReportView.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T12:48:17.287743Z","id":"40bb0bcc1668a0d75cc5d4c31479fe8f59581f02fa8c64aa0a726cc5f91b8f10","body":{"detail":"POST /api/queues/<qid>/reports/<tid>/claim and /release need an agent session (crates/clax-server/src/routes/queue_agent.rs agent_session, 400 no_session for a browser), so the report view offers neither. A person may still propose a fix or resolve a claimed report (both routes take a person with no lease), but cannot hand it back to the queue as open while the claimant's lease (clax_core::queue::LEASE_SECS) is live.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":45},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"cbfc89a20bf21ef2f49092c0580d85e8df636aff3e0fe5632e5c8735b4cdde72"},"suggested_fix":"Give triage persons a release that ends another holder's lease (audited as theirs), or show the lease's expiry with a note that the report reopens then.","summary":"A triage person cannot free a report an agent claimed: claim and release are agent-only, so a stale claim lasts until its lease runs out","tags":["queues","shell","triage","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/queues/ReportView.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T12:48:17.287811Z","id":"ebbac045e4cf72944b59b51ee7dbfffb4e8e2443383482dd748799dcd7829549","body":{"detail":"ReportView.svelte and QueueView.svelte (line 65) watch the gallery topic and reload on resync alone. A reply from the reporter or an agent, a fix an agent proposes or a verdict shows only after the person reloads the page or acts on the report (each action's answer is the report as it now is).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":112},"end":{"line":115},"content_hash":"6ff3b0f7e4f82e00a597c3f225b811ba75dcd7d8e2a6eeb99cb3e54ce60fc2dd"},"suggested_fix":"Subscribe to the report's thread events (or a queue topic) and refetch the report or the open tab on each.","summary":"The report and queue views refetch only when the stream resyncs, not when a report gets a comment, a fix or a verdict","tags":["queues","shell","live","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/queues/ReportView.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T12:48:17.287844Z","id":"4b0bbfef887c354f7a46bf56975206e00c955954d94d89b9665d1ed41267b8ff","body":{"detail":"The outlines place each omitted[].rect as a fraction of the image's naturalWidth and naturalHeight (tested by web/shell/src/queues/ReportView.test.ts 'outlines what the render left out, in the clip's own pixels'). web/sdk/src/types.ts:158 says the rect is 'in CSS pixels' and docs/contract.md names no unit. A context whose rect is in viewport CSS px (as filed by SDK builds that predate image-pixel rects) is outlined at the wrong place and size.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":148},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"55029f5feb5e80b48afc8bd482323b3cbddf0c386310d273eb9d2d8113e27afe"},"suggested_fix":"Say in web/sdk/src/types.ts and docs/contract.md (Context) that omitted[].rect is in the clip image's pixels from its top left corner, as the capture code produces it.","summary":"Omitted regions are outlined as rectangles in the clip image's own pixels, while web/sdk/src/types.ts still documents CaptureInfo.omitted as CSS pixels","tags":["queues","shell","capture","contract","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/queues/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T12:58:17.677591Z","id":"724149272beaceba2d68875c7d937560a8ca2ab8ad2e45e4c2c2abec97c121ba","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0ff19961e","summary":"countsText now names every state: '2 open · 1 claimed · 1 fix proposed · 1 verified · 1 resolved' (web/shell/src/queues/model.ts). bazel test //web:unit //web:e2e_queues PASSED at 0ff19961e (model.test.ts countReports cases, Queues.test.ts, e2e/queues.spec.ts '0 open · 0 claimed · 0 fix proposed · 0 verified · 1 resolved').","supersedes":"d4c62208b1db1435a628bd9f93926d49fa466fd1fc4408d0ba3e742d49376267","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
