{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/queues/ReportView.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:39.535374Z","id":"a3a5e330cc3e142ce40ea1948e630de27897da7a58ab95594ae2c7260e41e7b1","body":{"detail":"The outlines place each omitted[].rect as a fraction of the image's naturalWidth and naturalHeight (tested by web/shell/src/queues/ReportView.test.ts 'outlines what the render left out, in the clip's own pixels'). web/sdk/src/types.ts:158 says the rect is 'in CSS pixels' and docs/contract.md names no unit. A context whose rect is in viewport CSS px (as filed by SDK builds that predate image-pixel rects) is outlined at the wrong place and size.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":162},"end":{"line":166},"content_hash":"55029f5feb5e80b48afc8bd482323b3cbddf0c386310d273eb9d2d8113e27afe"},"suggested_fix":"Say in web/sdk/src/types.ts and docs/contract.md (Context) that omitted[].rect is in the clip image's pixels from its top left corner, as the capture code produces it.","summary":"Omitted regions are outlined as rectangles in the clip image's own pixels, while web/sdk/src/types.ts still documents CaptureInfo.omitted as CSS pixels","supersedes":"4b0bbfef887c354f7a46bf56975206e00c955954d94d89b9665d1ed41267b8ff","tags":["queues","shell","capture","contract","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/queues/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:57.822385Z","id":"3001ac0f6ddfea72271d5902a52ea2c234e234896b18b0aab2e8a5d7fc79d137","body":{"detail":"No route answers a queue's counts: Queue in the plan's shared shapes has none. web/shell/src/queues/Queues.svelte:37 runs countReports per queue on every load, fetching every report's comments to count them; past 20 pages the counts show with a '+'. A queue with many reports costs that many requests per visit.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"de487f71b845531a54b660d2aaf18a5b26e76eb7c7127f4c1cf2e01ab71f4a7a"},"suggested_fix":"Have GET /api/queues answer counts {open, claimed, resolved} per queue (one GROUP BY in the store) and show those.","summary":"Each queue's open/claimed/resolved counts are made by paging GET /api/queues/{qid}/reports in the browser, up to 20 pages per queue","supersedes":"db30d86895b2b63a4d809ed949c848bcc33633557ac7cb45b3f324e5e1bdd165","tags":["queues","perf","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/queues/ReportView.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T20:03:35.389211Z","id":"cfcb6991bdd188074203288c12cb32548f3da715301b8ecdd5423d40fed63907","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4b52f6332","summary":"Both views now watch queue:<qid> and refetch on its report events (filed, claimed, released, fixed, verified, reopened, resolved, commented on), on ready and on resync; the daemon publishes the event from publish_thread and the claim and release routes (crates/clax-server/src/routes/queue_agent.rs publish_report), to the queue's members alone. Evidence: bazel test //web:unit PASSED (ReportView.test.ts 'refetches when its queue's topic says it changed, keeping a reply draft and saying what changed', QueueView.test.ts 'refetches the tab in place when its queue's topic says a report changed'); //web:e2e_queues PASSED ('the triage views stay current: a filing, an agent's claim and a person's release show without a reload'); //crates/clax-server:all PASSED (api_queue_agent::a_queues_topic_tells_its_members_of_each_change_and_refuses_anyone_else, api_queue_reporter::a_filing_and_a_reporters_comment_reach_the_queues_topic).","supersedes":"4695ec23a134a5b450593e5d7e142994c6e90df107440cd16f073c174f5f0024","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/queues/ReportView.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T20:03:36.056039Z","id":"e4b8d366f58ac35780bcbb2e3420bdae86d5115f28d9e509d96f7dadfbfd59dd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ad36d9f13","summary":"A person now frees a claim: POST /api/queues/<qid>/reports/<tid>/release from a member who is not an agent ends whoever's live lease holds the report (Store::release_as_person, crates/clax-store/src/queues.rs), so the holder's next renew or fix is 409 lease_lost; it posts a triage-only note, wakes the holder (queue_event released) and records queue.release reason person. The report view offers 'Release claim' with a confirmation. Evidence: //crates/clax-server:all PASSED (api_queue_agent::a_member_releases_a_stale_claim_and_its_holder_is_told: non-member 404, member 200 open, renew/reply/fix 409 lease_lost, holder's wait gets queue_event released); //crates/clax-store:all PASSED (feedback::tests::a_persons_release_ends_the_claim_and_wakes_its_holder_alone); //web:unit and //web:e2e_queues PASSED.","supersedes":"6902dba2e63abfe256164d8c187d06782e9b16c326ac88e977426ad3f05308e9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
